NAME
    snapshot - capture and manage full memory space snapshots

SYNOPSIS
    snapshot <space> <name>
    snapshot list
    snapshot remove <name>

DESCRIPTION
    Saves a copy of memory space <space>'s entire current contents in
    shell state under <name>, allowing later byte-level comparisons with
    diff(1). Refuses spaces backed by live hardware registers with read
    side effects (such as CpuBus).

OPTIONS
    <space> <name>
        Capture the current contents of <space> under <name>, replacing
        any existing snapshot with the same name.

    list
        List all saved snapshots with their memory space and byte size.

    remove <name>
        Delete the saved snapshot named <name>.

EXAMPLES
    snapshot WRAM before
    snapshot list
    diff before
    snapshot remove before

EXIT STATUS
    0   Operation completed (or usage/refusal message printed).
    1   No target attached, unknown space, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    diff(1), search(1), dump(1), spaces(1)
